    text g_ya "to me" #8f887c x 730 y 510 font_size 50 hidden true
    text p_ty "ты" #2f6b8f say ты x 170 y 380 font_size 68 hidden true
    text a_ty "→" #8f887c x 290 y 380 font_size 56 hidden true
    text f_ty "тебе́" #3d3833 say тебе x 450 y 380 font_size 88 hidden true
    text g_ty "to you" #8f887c x 730 y 380 font_size 50 hidden true
    text p_vy "вы" #2f6b8f say вы x 170 y 250 font_size 68 hidden true
    text a_vy "→" #8f887c x 290 y 250 font_size 56 hidden true
    text f_vy "вам" #3d3833 say вам x 450 y 250 font_size 88 hidden true
    text g_vy "to you (polite)" #8f887c x 730 y 250 font_size 50 hidden true
    group table members ["p_ya","a_ya","f_ya","g_ya","p_ty","a_ty","f_ty","g_ty","p_vy","a_vy","f_vy","g_vy"] hidden true

    card title "I like it"

A: How do you say in Russian that you like something, say, coffee?
    draw tom i_coffee

A: In English, I do the liking, just as in я хочу́ ко́фе, I do the wanting.
    draw arrow_en en_line

B: Russian turns it round: мне нра́вится ко́фе.
    draw g_like

    erase arrow_en

B: Word for word: to me, it pleases, coffee. The coffee does the pleasing.
    draw arrow_ru

A: And мне, to me, is the one who's pleased: not I like it, but it pleases me.
    highlight g_like_w_1 color #c9871a effect underline

    erase tom i_coffee arrow_ru en_line g_like

A: That's why the thing you like keeps its plain form. Watch a book.
    draw s_read

A: In lesson fourteen, a book I read was кни́гу: я чита́ю кни́гу.
    highlight s_read color #c9871a part у$ effect underline

    draw s_book

B: But a book that pleases stays кни́га: мне нра́вится кни́га.
    highlight s_book color #c9871a part а$ effect underline

    erase s_read s_book

B: The same with my city: мне нра́вится Москва́, I like Moscow.
    draw i_city s_moscow

B: Москва́ stays Москва́, not Москву́ as after я ви́жу.
    highlight s_moscow color #c9871a part Москва́ effect underline

    hide i_city

A: With more than one thing, the verb changes too: мне нра́вятся коты́, I like cats.
    draw cats s_cats

B: One city pleases: нра́вится.
    highlight s_moscow color #c9871a part нра́вится effect underline

A: Many cats please: нра́вятся, with я where нра́вится has и. The green says more than one, just like коты́.
    highlight s_cats color #c9871a part нра́вятся effect underline

    erase s_moscow s_cats cats

A: Now, who is pleased. For я, it's мне: to me.
    draw p_ya a_ya f_ya g_ya

B: To a friend, ты becomes тебе́: тебе́ нра́вится Москва́? Do you like Moscow?
    draw p_ty a_ty f_ty g_ty

A: And to a customer, вы becomes вам, as a waiter asks: вам нра́вится суп?
    draw p_vy a_vy f_vy g_vy

    erase table

    text s_ne "Мне не нра́вится суп." #3d3833 say "Мне не нравится суп." x 500 y 470 font_size 64

B: Two small words finish it. Не, before the verb: мне не нра́вится суп, I don't like soup.
    highlight s_ne color #c9871a part ^не$ effect underline

    text s_och "Мне о́чень нра́вится ко́фе." #3d3833 say "Мне очень нравится кофе." x 500 y 300 font_size 64

A: And о́чень means very: мне о́чень нра́вится ко́фе, I like coffee very much.
    highlight s_och color #c9871a part о́чень effect underline

    erase s_ne s_och

B: Now Tom is visiting me in Moscow, so we talk about what we like.
    show speakers

    dialogue talk speakers.a tom speakers.b masha turns [{"by":"b","text":"Том, тебе́ нра́вится Москва́?","gloss":"Tom, do you like Moscow?"},{"by":"a","text":"Да! Мне о́чень нра́вится Москва́.","gloss":"Yes! I like Moscow very much."},{"by":"a","text":"А тебе́ нра́вится чай?","gloss":"And do you like tea?"},{"by":"b","text":"Нет, мне не нра́вится чай.","gloss":"No, I don't like tea."},{"by":"a","text":"А что тебе́ нра́вится?","gloss":"So what do you like?"},{"by":"b","text":"Мне нра́вится молоко́. И мне о́чень нра́вятся коты́.","gloss":"I like milk. And I really like cats."}] size 1.4

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

A: Milk again, and cats: more than one, so Masha said нра́вятся.
    highlight talk_6_words color #c9871a part нра́вятся effect underline

    erase talk

    hide speakers

    cards match size 1.4 y 475
        * "мне" match "to me"
        * "тебе́" match "to you (friend)"
        * "вам" match "to you (polite)"

    ask "Match each word to its meaning." on match store m reveal_style morph stage own voice a test t1
        intro: Five questions now, then your score.
        right: Мне is to me, тебе́ to a friend, and вам to someone you'd call вы.
        wrong: You got {m} on the first try.

    erase match

    quiz "Masha loves cats: Мне о́чень … коты́. Which word fills the gap?" store q2 reveal.text "Мне о́чень нра́вятся коты́." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 330 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Коты́ are more than one, so the verb counts them.
        wrong: How many cats are pleasing her?
        * нра́вится
        + нра́вятся
        * хочу́

    icon tc1 size 100 set twemoji x 400 y 540 or ["cat face"] icon_look picture of cat
    icon tc2 size 100 set twemoji x 500 y 540 or ["cat face"] icon_look picture of cat
    icon tc3 size 100 set twemoji x 600 y 540 or ["cat face"] icon_look picture of cat
    parallel true

    pause 0.8

    erase tc1 tc2 tc3 q2_stamp

    quiz "Say you like the book: Мне нра́вится … Which form fills the gap?" store q3 reveal.text "Мне нра́вится кни́га." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 330 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: The book does the pleasing, so it keeps its plain form.
        wrong: Кни́гу was for a book being read. Who does the pleasing here?
        + кни́га
        * кни́гу
        * кни́ги

    icon q_book size 130 set twemoji x 500 y 540 or ["green book","books"] icon_look picture of "closed book"

    pause 0.8

    erase q_book q3_stamp

    ask "Say you like Moscow: … нра́вится Москва́. Type the word for \"to me\"." answer ["мне"] store q4 default мне reveal.text "Мне нра́вится Москва́." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 330 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        keys: АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЦЧШЩЫЬЭЮЯ
        right: Moscow pleases me: мне нра́вится Москва́.
        wrong: Three letters: the form of я.

    draw i_city

    pause 0.8

    erase i_city q4_stamp

    quiz "What does Мне не нра́вится суп mean?" store q5 reveal.text "Мне не нра́вится суп." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 330 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: The soup doesn't please me: I don't like soup.
        wrong: Хочу́ would be want. And мне is the one pleased, not the soup.
        + I don't like soup.
        * I don't want soup.
        * Soup doesn't like me.

    icon q_soup size 130 set twemoji x 500 y 540 or ["bowl with spoon"] icon_look picture of "pot of food"

    pause 0.8

    erase q_soup q5_stamp

    show tom i_coffee arrow_ru g_like

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

A: So in Russian, what you like does the pleasing: it keeps its plain form, and the verb counts it.
    highlight arrow_ru color #c9871a

    erase g_like

A: And my answer to the opening question: мне о́чень нра́вится ко́фе. Пока́!
    draw s_bye

